target: skills/review/review-loop/stop-hook.test.sh
verify: bash skills/review/review-loop/stop-hook.test.sh
expect: an assertion vanished
why:    an assertion that VANISHES is invisible without a count, and it has happened twice here: a syntax error inside a `cond && ok || bad` list abandons the whole list so NEITHER branch runs, and six assertions appended below a suite's summary-and-exit never executed at all. shellcheck flags that idiom ~109 times across these suites and cannot tell a deliberate one from a broken one. This entry deletes one assertion that runs with or without looper and requires the count guard to notice — without it the suite reports "all checks passed" one check lighter, which is exactly the silent hole the guard exists to close. It targeted learn.test.sh until that suite went with learn.py; the guard is the same in every suite, so it moved rather than went.
--- old
[ ! -e "$TMP/empty.jsonl" ] \
	&& ok "hook exits before touching the store" || bad "hook exits before touching the store"
--- new
